gm-method/rendering (making flat instanced grass look lush like FluffyGrass, witnessed safe): the biggest lushness gap is a flat 3-vertex single-triangle blade - it can only PIVOT at the tip (wind keyed on position.y moves only the one raised vertex), reads spiky + sparse. FIX (geometry, one shared geo, instanced perf unchanged): rebuild the blade as a MULTI-SEGMENT (N=4-5 vertical quad rows = 2*(N+1) verts) tapered ribbon with a baked quadratic rest-curve (x += curve*v*v, v=y/height) - now the blade BENDS along its length and a quadratic wind bend (gv*gv) arcs the upper segments. Keep two crossed quads for silhouette volume. CRITICAL: recompute boundingSphere/Box for the taller curved bounds or perObjectFrustumCulled culls wrong. SHADER canopy lighting (additive, safe, inside the existing onBeforeCompile so the single program-cache-key is preserved): (1) base AO - deepen the lowest ~20% (gAO=0.6+0.4*smoothstep(0,0.2,vY)) so clumps read volumetric; (2) bias the shading normal toward world-up (mix(normal,(0,1,0),0.6) at normal_fragment_begin) for a soft even canopy wrap vs flat per-facet light. RISKIER, gate behind verification: flow-field wind + distance fade need per-instance WORLD-XZ, but @three.ez/instanced-mesh uses a TEXTURE-based per-instance matrix NOT a standard instanceMatrix attribute - verify the injected-chunk access path first or it no-ops/breaks the program; and replacing a hardcoded brightness *2.0 with scene-aware exposure needs a grass-vs-terrain brightness witness. Placement/determinism live in a separate GrassPlacement module - geometry+shader changes don't touch it. Witness: blade vertex count rose (6->24), instances still render, no pageerror.